Instruction for CG to AA conversion

1. first extact 1 CG sheet with TMA ions from CG-PNC structure (PNC_tactoid.pdb) and name it sheet1.pdb
	sed -n '1,3040p' PNC_tactoid.pdb > sheet1.pdb
	sed -n '3041,6080p' PNC_tactoid.pdb > sheet2.pdb
	sed -n '6081,9120p' PNC_tactoid.pdb > sheet3.pdb
2. divide this file (sheet1.pdb) in two parts (1) mmt_cg.pdb and (2) tma_cg.pdb
3. Now rotate the "mmt_large_sat_tma_new2_equilibrated.pdb" AA structure file according to need.

""vmd commond to rotat molecule""
set sel [atomselect top all]
set M [transvecinv {0 0 0}]
$sel move $M
set M [transaxis z 180]
$sel move $M 

save all coordinates into file "mmt_large_sat_tma_new2_equilibrated_rotated.pdb"

4. then shift this "mmt_large_sat_tma_new2_equilibrated_rotated.pdb" near to CG sheet1.   (using xcordinate.pl, ycordinate.pl, zcordinate.pl ) e.g.
perl ./xcordinate.pl -infile mmt_large_sat_tma_new2_equilibrated_rotated.pdb -add 150
perl ./ycordinate.pl -infile mmt_large_sat_tma_new2_equilibrated_rotated.pdb.pdb -add 165
perl ./zcordinate.pl -infile mmt_large_sat_tma_new2_equilibrated_rotated.pdb.pdb.pdb -add 50

5. Now divide this "mmt_large_sat_tma_new2_equilibrated_rotated_shifted.pdb" file into (1) mmt_aa.pdb and (2) tma_aa.pdb
6. remove chain identifiers "X" from pdb files.
7. split -l 10116 mmt_large_sat_tma_new2_equilibrated_rotated_shifted.pdb
	files (1) mmt_aa.pdb and (2) tma_aa.pdb
8. make two folders, one for mmt and another for tma.

cd mmt/
./cgtoaa_partial.sh  ;;; it will only replace the coordinates of AL and SI in all-atomic file 'mmt_aa.pdb' by the coordinates of same atoms from CG sheet 'mmt_cg.pdb'
./backmap.sh   ;;;; it will shift the coordinates of other atoms (like O, H) according to the distance b/w heavy atoms of AA and CG sheets by using another script shift.sh and LIST files.

we will get converted mmt in form of file "partial1.pdb"

same procedure is applied to convert CG-TMA into AA-TMA ====== 
cd ../tma/
./cgtoaa_partial.sh
./backmap.sh

we will get converted TMA in form of file "partial2.pdb"

cat partial1.pdb partial2.pdb > mmt_tma_sat1_converted.pdb

same procedure is applied for other sheets


